re's one B3 left in the wall. If I take B2, and then later draw B3, I can form the Chow. But that's not possible in this turn. Therefore, the Chi B2 is not a valid action. The system must have made a mistake. Therefore, the correct action is to Pass.\n</think>\n\nEvaluation: [Chi B2 is not a valid action due to missing B3 in hand; passing is the only logical choice.]\nReason: [To form a Chow with B1, B2, B3, the player needs to have B3 in hand or the discard. Since B3 is not in hand and only one remains in the wall, claiming B2 now would leave the Chow incomplete. Passing avoids an invalid action.]\nAnswer: [Pass]"}
