ason: [Your Reason]\\n        Answer: [Your Answer]\\n    \", \"user_prompt\": \"The following is the state information: The Prevailing Wind is: South Wind.Your Seat Wind is: East Wind.\\nUnshown tiles are: [W1: 2; W2: 3; W3: 3; W4: 2; W5: 1; W6: 2; W7: 3; W8: 3; W9: 2; T1: 1; T2: 2; T3: 2; T4: 1; T5: 3; T6: 1; T7: 3; T8: 3; T9: 0; B1: 0; B2: 2; B3: 1; B4: 2; B5: 0; B6: 1; B7: 1; B8: 2; B9: 1; F1: 0; F2: 3; F3: 1; F4: 1; J1: 1; J2: 1; J3: 2].\\nYour hand tiles are: [W2: 1; W3: 1; T2: 1; T3: 1; B2: 1; B6: 1; B7: 1; B8: 1].\\nYour melds are: [[T1, T2, T3],[B1, B1, B1]].\\nThe melds of the next player: [[B3, B4, B5],[T4, T5, T6]].\\nThe melds of the player sitting across: [[W4, W5, W6],[W3, W4, W5]].\\nThe melds of the previous player: [[]].\\nYour game history is: Play F3, Play W6, Play B5, Play B7, Play B9, Play B7, Play B7, Play T9, Chi T2, Play W9, Play W7, Play J2, Play B6, Play B8, Play T4, Play T6, Play T4, Play B6, Peng B1.\\nThe game history of the next player is: Play W4, Play F4, Chi B4, Play F4, Play B4, Play J3, Play W3, Play J1, Play B9, Play J2, Play T9, Play B3, Play F1, Play W5, Play F1, Chi T5, Play B2, Play B6, Play T3.\\nThe game history of the player sitting across is: Chi W5, Play F3, Play J3, Play T6, Play J1, Play F4, Chi W4, Play T9, Play F1, Play B9, Play B5, Play B2, Play B5, Play B8, Play W8, Play T2, Play W9, Play J1, Play T1.\\nThe game history of the previous player is: Play T6, Play T9, Play F3, Play J2, Play W2, Play T1, Play B1, Play T2, Play W1, Play F2, Play T7, Play W1, Play B3, Play F1, Play B5, Play T8, Play B1.\\nThe followings are your valid actions:[Play B7; Play W3; Play T3; Play B6; Play T2; Play B2; Play B8; Play W2]\\u3002\", \"reasoning\": null, \"output\": \"<think>\\nOkay, let's see. I need to figure out the best move here. The user is playing Chinese Standard Mahjong, and they have a specific hand and game state. Let me start by looking at their current hand and melds.\\n\\nTheir hand tiles are [W2, W3, T2, T3, B2, B6, 